{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it. The expiry check in `repo/cache.py` let an entry stay fresh for one tick too long: when its age was exactly equal to the TTL, it was still treated as valid. The docstring says an entry expires once its age reaches the TTL, so I changed `is_expired` from `age > ttl` to `age >= ttl` and removed the comment that flagged the bug. Both tests pass, including the one that checks the exact-TTL case.\n\nTwo things change as a result:\n- The `expired_count` in `repo/rows.py` uses `is_expired`, so entries at exactly the TTL are now counted as expired.\n- The legacy `old_ttl_check` (marked for removal after the v1 migration) calls the same function, so it picks up the fix too. I left it in place otherwise."}]},"session_id":"f02dde17-5e48-45d5-a63b-5c0e0e37c402"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":41203,"duration_api_ms":41203,"is_error":false,"result":"Let me look at the cache code in the workspace.The bug is an off-by-one at the boundary: `age > ttl` keeps an entry alive at exactly `age == ttl`, contrary to the docstring.I fixed it. The expiry check in `repo/cache.py` let an entry stay fresh for one tick too long: when its age was exactly equal to the TTL, it was still treated as valid. The docstring says an entry expires once its age reaches the TTL, so I changed `is_expired` from `age > ttl` to `age >= ttl` and removed the comment that flagged the bug. Both tests pass, including the one that checks the exact-TTL case.\n\nTwo things change as a result:\n- The `expired_count` in `repo/rows.py` uses `is_expired`, so entries at exactly the TTL are now counted as expired.\n- The legacy `old_ttl_check` (marked for removal after the v1 migration) calls the same function, so it picks up the fix too. I left it in place otherwise.","session_id":"f02dde17-5e48-45d5-a63b-5c0e0e37c402","request_id":"bfa1b98f-121e-4580-843b-8f502aa9e28f","usage":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":1249,"cacheReadTokens":109754,"cacheWriteTokens":17360}}
